sysutils/atuin: import atuin-18.24.8

Atuin replaces your existing shell history with a SQLite database and
records extra context (exit code, cwd, duration, host, session) for each
command.  It offers a full-screen fuzzy history search (bound to ctrl-r
and the up arrow) and optional end-to-end encrypted sync between machines
through a self-hosted or hosted Atuin server.

This package provides both the atuin client and the atuin-server daemon,
with an rc.d script (atuin-serverd) and a dedicated _atuin user for the
server.

Atuin captures everything you do in your terminal, from all your agentic
AI work, to all your terminal history, enabling you to:

   Let your agents see things you've worked on today, yesterday,
   a month or a year ago.

   Gain context on any work you've ever done in the terminal.
   If it happened in a terminal, Atuin lets you see it!

   Optionally, securely, sync your shell history and AI sessions across all
   your machines.

Atuin is secure by design, even when syncing: everything it syncs is
end-to-end encrypted, and nobody (including you, if you forget the key)
can decrypt it.
